          (stories/shapka-v-parke.yaml); media/words.jsonl AND
          media/labels.jsonl rows for all three sentence ids carry the same
          marks (the TTS followed the marks, so audio is baked wrong);
          lexicon/stories202611.jsonl `ru.lex.stories202611.baton` reading
          "ба́тон" is the vocab surface the reviewer flagged.
          EXTRA (beyond the ledger, added to FIX-M1-CONTENT-RU-001 scope):
          the p34 media rows spell сто́ит while the sentence text says
          стои́т, and labels.jsonl tags пла́чу as `dat.sg` — the
          audio-alignment rows are internally inconsistent beyond the stress
          fix itself.
        D-009: lexicon/verbs.jsonl — `ja.lex.verbs.kaerimasu` primary form
          かえりざく (+ kanji 返り咲く, reading kaerizaku) under gloss
          "to go back; to come back"; `ja.lex.verbs.arukimasu` primary
          あるきだす under gloss "to walk"; `ja.lex.verbs.nemasu` primary
          ねかす (+ 寝かす) under gloss "to sleep; to go to bed".
          Loanword case: lexicon/entertainment.jsonl `ja.lex.ent.konsaato`
          primary form こんさーと, used by sentences/entries.jsonl
          `ja.sent.concert-fun`; the pack writes loanwords in katakana
          (sentence shards: コーヒー x5, テレビ x3, パン x2 vs こんさーと x3).
          Provenance days re-measured from the raw logs: かえりざく first in
          lesson_plan day 14 (14 days), あるきだす day 14 (14 days), ねかす
          day 17 (7 days) -> "day 14-17 lesson_plan" holds. Precision note:
          返り咲く/かえりざく IS a real Japanese word ("return to one's
          former glory") — it is simply not the verb the id and gloss
          promise; D-009 wording corrected accordingly.
        D-010 REPRODUCED (this was the pre-dispatch gate for
          FIX-M1-CONTENT-JA-001). practice_task item
          `ja.lex.greetings.oyasumi-nasai#recall-meaning` carries slots
          [{text:"おやすみ", label:"the rest wish"}, {text:"なさい",
          alternatives:["なさい","ませ"], label:"the polite ending",
          target:true}] — observed on sim days 13, 14, 19. Root cause pinned
          in DATA, not the engine: that exact `slots` array (label "the rest
          wish") is stored in languages/ja-JP/lexicon/greetings.jsonl. So it
          is a corrupted morpheme label on ONE surface, not an item "split
          across two practice_task surfaces" as the reviewer lane inferred.
          Learner-visible junk English confirmed -> severity raised
          known-limit -> fix, disposition FIX-M1-CONTENT-JA-001.

